# Configuration for logitech-flow-kvm service
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/logitech-flow-kvm/config and customize for your machine.
#
# Custom virtual environment path (optional, defaults to ~/.local/share/logitech-flow-kvm/venv):
# LOGITECH_FLOW_KVM_VENV="$HOME/.local/share/logitech-flow-kvm/venv"

# Arguments to pass to logitech-flow-kvm when started via systemd service.
# Run 'logitech-flow-kvm list-devices' to identify device serial numbers and slot IDs.
#
# Server (Primary / Leader machine):
# Starts the server tracking the keyboard as leader (slot 1) and follower devices (mouse).
# Use --hostname so the TLS certificate includes the server's local domain name.
# LOGITECH_FLOW_KVM_ARGS="flow-server --hostname pisa.lan 1 <KEYBOARD_SERIAL> <MOUSE_SERIAL>"
#
# Client (Follower / Secondary machine):
# Connects to the primary machine's hostname or IP address on slot 2:
# LOGITECH_FLOW_KVM_ARGS="flow-client 2 pisa.lan"

LOGITECH_FLOW_KVM_ARGS=""
